#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:10
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:12
msgid ""
"Teach agents how to use Hero's cross-repo peering protocol — the three-"
"tier ladder (advisory peer call, spec-out peer call, async handoff) plus "
"the convention-import fallback — so work that crosses a sibling "
"workspace's surface gets the protocol's provenance for free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:14
msgid ""
"The full protocol convention lives at `.hero/knowledge/conventions"
"/peering-protocol.md`. Read it once for depth. This skill is the agent-"
"facing operational distillation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:16
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:18
msgid "Load me when any of these are true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:20
msgid ""
"The user names a sibling repo by alias (\"ask hero-code\", \"hand off to "
"hero-cloud\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:21
msgid ""
"The user describes a question whose answer lives in a sibling's surface "
"(\"what's their error envelope?\", \"does this break X?\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"The active spec touches files whose contract is owned by a sibling (see "
"`hero context` for contract-import surfacing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"The work being asked for is genuinely a sibling's responsibility and the "
"user hasn't called it out yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:25
msgid ""
"Don't load me for purely local work, even if a sibling repo exists in the"
" workspace's `repos` config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:27
msgid "The three-tier ladder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"Pick the **least invasive mode that resolves the work**. Don't escalate "
"when an advisory call would suffice; don't drop to convention import when"
" a handoff would close the loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Writes?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Pick when"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "**Sync peer call: advisory**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Nothing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"You need a fact — \"what's X's shape?\", \"is there already an endpoint "
"for this?\", \"does this break you?\". Peer investigates, returns "
"findings text, writes nothing on its side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "**Sync peer call: spec-out**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Spec on peer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"You realized the work is genuinely the peer's — its conventions should "
"kick in. Peer's Hero designs the spec natively on its side and returns "
"the slug; your local spec moves to `awaiting_peer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "**Async handoff**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Spec on peer (scaffolded)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"You already did the investigation; the fix clearly belongs to the peer "
"and you want it on their queue. Your local spec moves to `handed_off`; "
"theirs lands as `planning` with `received_from:` provenance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "**Convention import (fallback)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Work legitimately stays in your workspace but must respect the peer's "
"surface (e.g. a serializer producing a payload they parse). Pull the "
"peer's peer-surface conventions into context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:38
msgid "Full-delivery peer call (peer designs AND delivers) is v2. Not available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:40
msgid "Decision tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:42
msgid ""
"Does the user already know the answer is on the peer's side?\n"
"├─ Yes, and they did the investigation → ASYNC HANDOFF\n"
"├─ Yes, but they want peer's conventions to shape the design → SPEC-OUT\n"
"└─ No, they need to learn something first → ADVISORY\n"
"\n"
"Then ask: does the work itself stay on our side once we know the answer?\n"
"├─ Yes, but it crosses peer's surface → CONVENTION IMPORT (after "
"advisory)\n"
"└─ No, it should move → ESCALATE to spec-out or handoff\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:53
msgid ""
"When the user's intent is genuinely ambiguous between two modes, **ask "
"one focused clarifying question** rather than guessing. Example: \"Want "
"hero-cloud to design the migration, or just a quick read on whether this "
"breaks their schema?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:55
msgid "Composing a good peer-call prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:57
msgid ""
"A peer call spawns a subagent in the peer's workspace with its full Hero "
"context loaded. Treat it like sending a colleague a focused brief — not "
"paraphrasing the user verbatim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:59
msgid "Required elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:61
msgid ""
"**The specific question or task** — name the artifact, the field, the "
"constraint. Bad: \"what about the error format?\" Good: \"What's the "
"current shape of the `errors` array in the `/v1/order` POST response? Any"
" deprecations in flight?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:62
msgid ""
"**The reason** (`--reason \"...\"`) — what's happening on your side that "
"prompted the call. Helps the peer subagent triage urgency and rank "
"against in-flight work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:63
msgid ""
"**The related spec** (`--related-spec <slug>`) — when there's an active "
"spec driving the call, attach it. The peer's trail and your local handoff"
" record link to it; cross-repo `hero why` can walk the chain later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:65
msgid "Mode flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:67
msgid ""
"`--mode=advisory` — read-only investigation. Default budget: 20 turns / "
"50,000 tokens. Use `--budget-turns` / `--budget-tokens` to override."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:68
msgid ""
"`--mode=spec-out` — peer designs a spec. Default budget: 50 turns / "
"150,000 tokens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:70
msgid "Prompt shape — advisory mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:72
msgid ""
"hero peer call <alias> --mode=advisory \\\n"
"  --related-spec <active-slug> \\\n"
"  --reason \"Why this call is happening on our side\" \\\n"
"  \"Specific question. Concrete. Mention the file/symbol/field you care "
"about.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:79
msgid "Prompt shape — spec-out mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:81
msgid ""
"hero peer call <alias> --mode=spec-out \\\n"
"  --related-spec <active-slug> \\\n"
"  --reason \"Why peer should design this rather than us\" \\\n"
"  \"Design the [thing]. Constraints: <list>. Out of scope: <list>. "
"Acceptance shape: <list>.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:88
msgid ""
"The peer's `/design` flow runs on this prompt. Treat it like a `/design` "
"kickoff brief — clearer the better."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:90
msgid "Anti-patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:92
msgid "Don't:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:94
msgid ""
"**Paraphrase the user's words verbatim** as the peer-call prompt. The "
"peer's subagent needs a structured question, not a chat fragment. "
"Translate intent into a specific brief."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:95
msgid ""
"**Make a peer call when the answer is in your own workspace.** Check "
"`hero search` and `hero relevant` first. Peer calls cost a subagent "
"spawn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:96
msgid ""
"**Skip `--related-spec` when one exists.** The trail breaks; cross-repo "
"`hero why` can't walk the chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:97
msgid ""
"**Use spec-out when advisory would resolve it.** Spec-out writes a spec "
"on the peer's side; advisory writes nothing. Escalate only when the work "
"genuinely belongs to the peer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:98
msgid ""
"**Use handoff to dump unfinished investigation on the peer.** Handoff is "
"for *completed* investigations where the fix clearly belongs to the peer."
" If you haven't found the cause yet, do advisory first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:99
msgid ""
"**Run multiple peer calls when one would do.** Bundle questions in a "
"single advisory call when they're related."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:100
msgid ""
"**Wait synchronously on a handoff** — handoff is async by design. Your "
"local spec moves to `handed_off`; you continue other work. The status "
"auto-flips to `handed_back` when peer completes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:102
msgid "Async handoff — when and how"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:104
msgid "Use handoff when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:106
msgid "You've diagnosed the root cause and it's on the peer's side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:107
msgid ""
"The peer should own the fix end-to-end (their conventions, their PR, "
"their merge)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:108
msgid ""
"You can scope the handoff well enough to scaffold a useful spec on their "
"side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:110
msgid ""
"hero handoff <local-slug> <peer-alias> \\\n"
"  --reason \"Symptom in our workspace, root cause in peer's surface\" \\\n"
"  --type bug\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:116
msgid "Your local spec moves through these states:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "`handed_off`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Just dropped on peer's queue. Receiver scaffold landed; trail entry "
"written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "`awaiting_peer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Peer's spec is `delivering`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "`handed_back`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Peer's spec is `completed`. Verify the symptom is gone on your side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:124
msgid ""
"When the peer completes, status auto-flips on next `hero status` run. To "
"pick up:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:126
msgid "hero handoff accept <slug>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:130
msgid "Then verify the original symptom resolved before marking your spec done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:132
msgid "Convention import — the fallback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:134
msgid ""
"Use when the work legitimately stays on your side but must respect a "
"peer's surface. Example: a JSON serializer in your workspace producing a "
"payload the peer parses; you can't escape knowing their schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:136
msgid "hero relevant --peer <alias> --surface http-response\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:140
msgid ""
"Pulls the peer's peer-surface conventions matching the surface tag into "
"your active context. Less powerful than a peer call (no investigation, no"
" new info), but free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:142
msgid "Discovery commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "Which peers are configured here?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero peer list`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "What's reachable? Manifests current?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero peer list` (output includes status)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "What does one peer expose?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero peer show <alias>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "What's in flight across the boundary?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero handoff status`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:151
msgid ""
"If `hero peer list` returns empty, peers aren't registered yet. Run `hero"
" admin repos add <alias> <path>` first (see `CROSS-REPO-PEERING.md`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:153
msgid "Output discipline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:155
msgid ""
"After a peer call returns, **summarize the findings for the user before "
"acting on them**. The peer's response is a structured block; the user "
"wants the headline plus the actionable shape, not the raw envelope. Quote"
" relevant excerpts in your reply; don't dump the full peer response "
"unless asked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:157
msgid ""
"After a handoff, **confirm the trail wrote** (`hero handoff status` shows"
" the entry) and tell the user the peer-side slug + which side now owns "
"the next move. Don't pretend the handoff is the work — it's the start of "
"work happening elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:159
msgid "Related"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:161
msgid ""
"Convention: `.hero/knowledge/conventions/peering-protocol.md` — the full "
"protocol with edge cases and v2 directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:162
msgid ""
"Decision: `.hero/knowledge/decisions/cross-repo-peering-local-first.md` —"
" why local-first by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:163
msgid ""
"Setup guide: `CROSS-REPO-PEERING.md` (workspace root) — one-time "
"registration and config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md:164
msgid ""
"Slash command: `/peer` — structured front door for peer call / handoff / "
"list / show."
msgstr ""

